  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43797838",
      "title": "Extracting Values with Two-Way-Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 80,
      "videoOrder": 74,
      "sourceHash": "3cc3a976f127d2c22b31e2e05d49882f9644342e48e244b20af91e6f97d4f6fc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.49,
          "en": "So let's set up two-Way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "for these inputs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "As you learned earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 10.98,
          "en": "this can be achieved by in the end, combining the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.98,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "and event binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "since two-Way binding is about binding both directions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 21.51,
          "en": "We want to be able to send data into the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.51,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "that we're binding and we want to be able to get values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.813,
          "en": "out of that element when the values change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.86,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "Now, you also learned earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "that there is no built-in property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "you could listen to on the standard browser elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 42.03,
          "en": "that would support two-Way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "Instead, you have to bring your own elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 48.69,
          "en": "and you will learn how to support two-Way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.69,
          "end": 51.54,
          "en": "on your own properties in your own components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.54,
          "end": 53.07,
          "en": "later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.07,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "but to unlock it for certain built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 58.32,
          "en": "like for the input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 61.65,
          "en": "you can use the NG model directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 64.14,
          "en": "which is provided by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.14,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "which does support two-way binding on input and text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 71.013,
          "en": "and related elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "Now, this NG model directive is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 79.68,
          "en": "if you do import this forms module, which we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 81.873,
          "en": "so we don't need to change anything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "And now we can use that two-way binding syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "which is square brackets around parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 91.203,
          "en": "around the property that you want to bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "And that NG model thing when used with two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "we'll now listen to changes of the value of this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "and then update some property of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "with that changed value, or if we change that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "from some other place in our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "it will send that data back into the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 116.07300000000001,
          "en": "So we'll have that two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "That of course also means that we now need a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 123.93,
          "en": "to which we can two-way bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.93,
          "end": 127.11,
          "en": "and therefore back in the user component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 129.75,
          "en": "I will now add a new property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.75,
          "end": 132.75,
          "en": "inside of the user input component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.75,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "and I'll name it entered initial investment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 140.403,
          "en": "Though of course the property name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "and I'll set this to an initial value of a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 147.183,
          "en": "that contains the number zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "So I'll not set it to the number zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 155.6,
          "en": "but to a string that contains the zero digit, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.64,
          "end": 159.54,
          "en": "And I'm doing this because as I mentioned earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "the value you'll get out of an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "will always be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "even if the user entered a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 168.24,
          "en": "it will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.24,
          "end": 171.57,
          "en": "It will be a string that includes the number, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 174.63,
          "en": "And that's why I'm also setting my initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.63,
          "end": 178.2,
          "en": "to such a string that includes a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "We'll convert it to an actual number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 183.723,
          "en": "which we need for our calculations later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.01,
          "end": 187.56,
          "en": "But that's the property to which I wanna bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.56,
          "end": 192.56,
          "en": "and here I am setting up this property to not use signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 195.57,
          "en": "You could also use signals here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.57,
          "end": 198.63,
          "en": "and I'll show you how to migrate the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.63,
          "end": 200.31,
          "en": "to signals later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.31,
          "end": 202.32,
          "en": "But for the moment, I'll use this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.32,
          "end": 204.333,
          "en": "and not use a Signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "But with that now added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 210.75,
          "en": "we can go back to the user input component, HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "and use this entered initial investment property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 216.96,
          "en": "as a value for the two-way binding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.96,
          "end": 218.883,
          "en": "for this first input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.56,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "Now, I'll press this code format shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 224.85,
          "en": "to make this a bit more readable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.85,
          "end": 227.613,
          "en": "and with that, my first input is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.63,
          "end": 230.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now of course, all the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.57999999999998,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "should be two-way bound though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 236.49,
          "en": "and therefore I'll repeat that process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 238.77,
          "en": "And in the user input component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 243.77,
          "en": "I'll also add an entered annual investment property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.62,
          "end": 248.643,
          "en": "which also contains zero as a starting value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.2,
          "end": 254.13,
          "en": "I'll add an entered expected return property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.13,
          "end": 259.13,
          "en": "which also has zero as a starting value, or maybe five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.38,
          "end": 263.5,
          "en": "Let's use 5% as a default expected return rate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.84,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "and a entered duration, which maybe has 10",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 272.25,
          "en": "as a starting value though also as a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.25,
          "end": 276.003,
          "en": "just as the expected return and the other properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.7,
          "end": 281.58,
          "en": "Now with all these properties added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "back in the user input component HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "we can copy this two-way binding code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 291.65999999999997,
          "en": "and add it on all those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.65999999999997,
          "end": 294.24,
          "en": "For example here, the annual investment input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.24,
          "end": 296.73,
          "en": "though of course, I now don't wanna bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.73,
          "end": 300.06,
          "en": "to the entered initial investment property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.06,
          "end": 304.563,
          "en": "but to the entered annual investment property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.3,
          "end": 308.49,
          "en": "And then again, we can copy this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.49,
          "end": 310.72,
          "en": "to the expected return input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 313.26,
          "end": 318.26,
          "en": "and bind this to the entered expected return property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.76,
          "end": 323.23,
          "en": "and copy it to the duration input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.3,
          "end": 327.843,
          "en": "and bind it to entered duration like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.32,
          "end": 336.08299999999997,
          "en": "With that, I added two way binding to all these inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 340.8,
          "en": "and therefore back in the user input component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 340.8,
          "end": 344.13,
          "en": "we can now also console log those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 344.13,
          "end": 347.943,
          "en": "to confirm that we really captured them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 348.81,
          "end": 352.263,
          "en": "So I'll output the entered initial investment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.46,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "This entered initial investment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 361.95,
          "en": "I'll output this entered annual investment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 361.95,
          "end": 366.3,
          "en": "and of course also the expected return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 366.3,
          "end": 368.403,
          "en": "and the entered duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 371.4,
          "end": 376.2,
          "en": "With that done, if you save this and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 376.2,
          "end": 380.58,
          "en": "you'll be greeted by an error here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 380.58,
          "end": 384.51,
          "en": "And the error message is that NG model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 384.51,
          "end": 386.43,
          "en": "if used within a foreign tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 386.43,
          "end": 388.71,
          "en": "in the end needs the name attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 388.71,
          "end": 391.08299999999997,
          "en": "on the input element to which you set it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 392.22,
          "end": 395.61,
          "en": "And that's not the case here in my template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 395.61,
          "end": 399.93,
          "en": "All these inputs have an ID attribute but no name attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 399.93,
          "end": 404.223,
          "en": "but NG model requires it as this error message tells us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 405.72,
          "end": 407.88,
          "en": "Well, that's not too difficult to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 407.88,
          "end": 410.1,
          "en": "We can of course simply add the name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 410.1,
          "end": 413.523,
          "en": "and set the name to the same value as the ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 414.78,
          "end": 417.48,
          "en": "So I did this here for the initial investment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 417.48,
          "end": 420.99,
          "en": "and all updated for all our inputs as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 420.99,
          "end": 424.59,
          "en": "So here, update the annual investment input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 424.59,
          "end": 425.943,
          "en": "to have the right name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 426.99,
          "end": 430.473,
          "en": "Then also here, the expected return input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 431.67,
          "end": 436.343,
          "en": "And last but not least, also the duration input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 439.92,
          "end": 442.98,
          "en": "And with those name attributes added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 442.98,
          "end": 445.68,
          "en": "now you see if I reload, the error is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 445.68,
          "end": 449.85,
          "en": "And if I now enter some values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 449.85,
          "end": 452.52,
          "en": "and maybe keep the defaults for expected return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 452.52,
          "end": 455.46,
          "en": "and duration, if I click calculate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 455.46,
          "end": 458.013,
          "en": "you see that data was received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 459.48,
          "end": 462.39,
          "en": "And we also see the two-way binding in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 462.39,
          "end": 464.73,
          "en": "because our entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 464.73,
          "end": 468.84000000000003,
          "en": "like the initial investment are captured and output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
